Flotilla
========

Flotilla is a fork of:

    tailsocks
    https://github.com/ItalyPaleAle/tailsocks
    Copyright (c) Alessandro (Ale) Segala
    Licensed under the MIT License — see LICENSE.md

Upstream code retained and used (with package renames):
  - main.go::setExitNodePrefs and the tsnet.Server boot dance
    → internal/worker/worker.go
  - auth.go (OAuth2 client credentials → ephemeral auth key minting)
    → internal/auth/oauth.go
  - resolver.go (Tailscale MagicDNS resolver + TTL cache)
    → internal/resolver/resolver.go
  - buildinfo/buildinfo.go
    → internal/buildinfo/buildinfo.go

Net-new in Flotilla:
  - cmd/flotilla            CLI with subcommands (run, init, ip, nodes, doctor)
  - internal/config         YAML config parser + validator
  - internal/pool           N-worker pool + Strategy interface (round_robin,
                            random, sticky, least_active, tagged)
  - internal/dispatcher     Front-end SOCKS5 + HTTP CONNECT dispatchers,
                            with request-level pin / tag / sticky hints
  - internal/admin          /health, /health/nodes, /ip, /metrics
  - internal/metrics        Prometheus collectors

The MIT license terms of the upstream apply to all retained code, and our
own additions are released under the same MIT terms.
